Employee Management System using
PagingAndSortingRepository
Scenario
A software company wants to develop an Employee Management System to manage employee
records efficiently. Since the company has thousands of employees, displaying all employee
records at once is not practical. Therefore, the application should support viewing employee
records page by page and sorting employees based on different fields such as salary and name.
Requirements
1. Create Employee Entity
Create an Employee class with the following fields:
private Integer employeeId;
private String employeeName;
private String department;
private Double salary;
2. Create Repository
Create an EmployeeRepository interface that extends:
PagingAndSortingRepository<Employee, Integer>
3. Service Requirements
View Employees with Pagination
Create a method: getEmployeesByPage(int pageNumber, int pageSize)
View Employees Sorted by Salary
Create a method: getEmployeesSortedBySalary()
View Employees Sorted by Name
Create a method: getEmployeesSortedByName()
4. Main Application
Insert at least 10 employee records into the database and perform the following operations:
1. Display Employee Records (Page 1, Size 3)
2. Display Employee Records (Page 2, Size 3)
3. Display Employees Sorted by Salary
4. Display Employees Sorted by Employee Name
